People often ask what tools I use while building projects.

Here's what's open on my computer almost every day:

• ChatGPT – Brainstorming ideas, solving roadblocks, and learning faster.

• VS Code – Where I build and experiment.

• GitHub – Version control and collaboration.

• Supabase – Managing databases and authentication without the usual headache.

• Cursor – My AI-powered code editor that has completely changed how I build.

• Oracle Cloud – Hosting and running the infrastructure behind my projects.

I've learned that productivity isn't about using every new tool that comes out.

It's about building a workflow you know inside out.

These are the tools that help me spend less time fighting my setup and more time actually building.

I'm always curious to discover better tools.

What's one tool you use almost every day that you couldn't work without?

